# Homebrew manifest for this machine, managed by brew-file (rcmdnk/file).
#
#   brew-file install                       # install everything listed here
#   brew file update                        # re-record what is installed
#
#
# brew-file (rcmdnk/file) manages this file: brew-wrap appends newly installed
# packages automatically on `brew install`. That means this file is REGENERATED,
# so the section comments below will not survive indefinitely.
#
# Two things to know:
#
#  1. brew-wrap runs `brew file update`, which by default records the full
#     dependency closure -- that is how this file previously reached 337 entries
#     including the whole Qt suite and openjdk. To keep it to top-level packages
#     only, without changing the workflow:  brew file set_leaves 1
#
#  2. Homebrew 6 refuses to load formulae from untrusted taps, and both
#     `brew leaves` and `brew bundle dump` OMIT them silently -- sketchybar and
#     borders included. brew.sh runs `brew trust` for the taps below first, so
#     keep that step or those entries will quietly disappear on regeneration.

